2.0.d - UNRELEASED
Adjusted - Random images now favour images that match the planet's features instead of images with many exclusions
Adjusted - The image selector lists the best matching images first
Fixed - Planets got no random image when every fitting image was already in use or none matched the exact colony size
Fixed - Images tagged for stations only as a required tag never showed up for stations
Fixed - Four station images never showed up because of tag typos, and one image could appear on hostile planets
Adjusted - Settings fall back to their defaults when a saved value is missing or invalid
Adjusted - The description editor has one text box per description: click to place the cursor, Enter starts a new line, and the box scrolls once the text is longer than it
Note - Each description holds up to 5000 characters
Fixed - Descriptions edited before the number of text lines was lowered were cut off
Fixed - Crash when TASC upgraded a station whose description was edited before the number of text lines was raised
Removed - The "Number of text lines" setting, the description editor no longer uses fixed lines

2.0.c
Adjusted - Switched out the image for Madeira
Fixed - Crash when editing the description of certain modded planets
Fixed - Disabling the image portion of the mod now actually works
Fixed - No longer crashes with TASC. This is an interim fix. Astropolis will not respect the Ill.Ent settings until TASC updates.

2.0.b
Adjusted - Changed the default of the "Add random images to NPC colonies" to false
Fixed - Random crash when a station did not have a custom entity type

2.0.a
Added - 0.98a compatibility
Added - ~1300 new images
Added - The mod now un-loads any unused images, making the VRAM use effectively zero (Thank you, starficz!)
Added - LunaLib integration
Added - Setting to entirely disable the image part of the mod
Added - Image picker now respects colony size and will try to find a fitting image for the population size
Added - Buttons to specify colony size matching when picking
Fixed - Picker now respects the seed for image picking / randomisation options
Fixed - The mod now properly classifies planets with hazard > 175 as "hostile environment"
Removed - The entire old image set of ~600 images
Removed - Some old settings that were confusing and never used

1.2.b
Adjusted - 0.97 compatibility

1.2.a
Added - setting specifying if the pre-set images overwrite the existing vanilla illustrations. off by default.
Adjusted - 0.96 compatibility
Fixed - Crash when abandoning a colony
Fixed - Custom set images are no longer lost on save reload
Fixed - Orbital Stations no longer have different visuals than planets until player leaves system
Fixed - Custom images now get retained when set via orbital station
Fixed - Custom images now immediately apply to orbital stations when leaving a planet

1.1.b
Adjusted - Now removes accidental double spaces on line breaks

1.1.a
Added - In-game overlay allowing you to change planet and colony descriptions and texts
Added - Setting to set the "Display duplicates" button to true by default
Fixed - Should now consistently apply illustrations to player owned planets without image
Fixed - Removed signature from image 12
Fixed - Added !cld tag to image 3

